WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.960
Speaker 1: I want to talk next about one of
the the real implications of this bogus Arizona

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.630
audit that's taking place of absentee ballots,
looking for bamboo fibers and all sorts of

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:12.950
other stuff.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:20.230
The the impact of the Arizona audit is not
going to be Joe Biden retroactively loses

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.689
Arizona.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:24.869
The impact of the Arizona audit is not going
to be.

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.769
Joe Biden is removed from the White House
and Trump is reinstated, to use the word that

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:32.870
they've been throwing around for the last
week or so.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.650
But there is going to be an impact from this
audit.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.710
And there's a really good article in NPR about
this by Miles Parks called Experts Call It

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.899
a clown show.

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:49.790
But Arizona audit is a disinformation blueprint,
explaining it's not an audit.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:55.329
It's an audit in name only, according to Matt
Masterson, a former Department of Homeland

00:00:55.329 --> 00:01:00.320
Security official who helped lead the election
security prep for the last election.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.710
He says it's a threat to the overall confidence
of democracy, all in pursuit of continuing

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.090
a narrative that we know to be a lie.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.060
This is a really important thing to understand.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.580
Maybe there are people who think the Arizona
audit and the search for bamboo fibers and

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.820
all of this stuff could lead to a change in
the Arizona results or a change in the 2020

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:22.820
results.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.360
Overall, it's not going to.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.530
But even without achieving that, it still
is achieving something that should be very

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:35.299
scary to all of us, which is it continues
to put in people's minds the idea that our

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:37.729
elections are just a free for all.

00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:41.920
They don't work when a candidate wins by millions
and millions of votes, maybe they actually

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.460
lost by millions and millions of votes.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.450
And it just further reinforces the idea that,
hey, the election results are sort of like

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.079
opinion, much the same way where you might
like one flavor bubble tea.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.930
And I like a different flavor.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:58.100
Or I might think that one type of cherry ice
cream is good.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.469
And you might say, no, Cherry Garcia is the
best one.

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:02.469
Right.

00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:04.840
It equates a position on abortion.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.210
Like what's my opinion about whether abortion
should or shouldn't be legal to who one is

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:13.730
just an opinion and we can challenge it and
we can use any mechanism that we can think

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.390
of to try to challenge that.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.310
That's the crisis that Matt Masterson is pointing
out here.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:26.739
Masterson says the strategy chosen by the
Arizona Republican state Senate leaders is

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:31.100
working as intended to undermine confidence
in the outcome of last year's vote.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.100
And this is the point.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.540
Even if it doesn't overturn it, it undermines
confidence in elections in general.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:43.019
The process is a simple exercise in how disinformation
spreads and takes hold.

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:47.180
In twenty twenty one, and experts fear it
presents a blueprint for other states and

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.019
lawmakers to follow one that's already showing
signs of being emulated across the country.

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:54.129
And this is the key line right here.

00:02:54.129 --> 00:03:00.280
Masterson says now we have a playbook out
there where if you don't like the results,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:05.100
by the way, in an election that wasn't particularly
close, you claim you didn't lose.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.870
And in fact, the process itself was rigged
against you.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.370
And the steps are first create a false reality.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.909
That's the first step.

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:19.140
The second step is hit the airwaves, which
they did very early and continue to do.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:26.239
The third step is used doubt to sow more doubt,
and then you go into next election with people

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:32.360
already primed to doubt whatever it is that
they hear from you, that is the three step

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.360
process.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.961
And unfortunately, I don't know if these people
are evil geniuses who are thinking, hey, you

00:03:37.961 --> 00:03:39.650
know what?

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:45.500
This Arizona thing is not going to accomplish
anything in terms of Arizona 2020, but this

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:51.280
is going to seed doubt and it'll create a
pretext for people to claim any election we

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.340
lose was fraudulent.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.780
I don't know that they're really evil geniuses
and they're thinking in those terms, but it

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.290
doesn't matter because that's the effect that
it has.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.400
And so much like I said in the last segment,
when we start seeing these new Trump rallies,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.740
supposedly later this month, maybe not until
July, when we start seeing them, what is going

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.660
to be the mood of the people in the crowd
about the legitimacy, the legitimacy of any

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.660
election?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.519
Because I believe that what we're going to
see here very clearly is, you know, Trump's

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:22.830
going to pick his favorites for 20, 22, and
maybe a whole bunch of them are going to lose.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:23.830
Maybe some will win.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.830
We don't yet know.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.060
But if they lose, yes, it hurts.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:32.400
Trump's shot at twenty twenty four if he can't
successfully be the kingmaker in twenty twenty

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.550
two.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:38.280
But does anybody have any doubt that they're
going to say, guys, listen, Democrats control

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.310
the House now.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:40.550
Democrats control the Senate.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.370
Joe Biden controls the White House.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.020
Of course they rigged it.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.250
Of course they rigged it.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.810
So it seems to me a foregone conclusion if
they don't get what they want in twenty, twenty

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:54.259
two, they're going to say it was all fraudulent.

00:04:54.259 --> 00:05:00.460
And the stuff they're doing now, including
in Arizona, is going to be used as a pretext

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:05.080
to gin up the idea that if you don't like
the results, it's totally legit now in American

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.840
politics to say the results were rigged.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.330
Very scary stuff.

